# DataPilotFlow Dashboard - Cursor Instructions

## Package Management
- **Use `npm` for package management** - This is a Node.js/TypeScript project
- To install dependencies: `npm install`
- To add a new dependency: `npm install <package-name>` or `npm install -D <package-name>` for dev dependencies
- Use `package.json` for dependency management

## Code Understanding Before Changes
- **ALWAYS read and understand existing code before making changes**
- Search for similar patterns in the codebase using `codebase_search` tool
- Review existing components, hooks, and API integrations before implementing new features
- Understand the React component structure and state management patterns
- Check existing patterns for API calls, error handling, and UI components

## React Best Practices
- Use functional components with hooks (not class components)
- Use TypeScript for all components and utilities
- Follow React best practices: proper key usage, memoization when needed, etc.
- Use proper state management (React Query for server state, useState for local state)

## TypeScript
- **Always use TypeScript** - no JavaScript files unless absolutely necessary
- Use proper types for all props, state, and function parameters
- Avoid `any` type - use proper types or `unknown`
- Use interfaces for object types, types for unions/intersections
- Use type guards when needed

## Component Structure
- Keep components focused and single-purpose
- Extract reusable logic into custom hooks
- Use proper component composition
- Follow the existing folder structure: `src/components/`, `src/pages/`, `src/api/`, etc.

## API Integration
- Use `react-query` (`@tanstack/react-query`) for API calls
- Use the existing API helper functions in `src/api/helpers.ts`
- Follow existing patterns for query hooks and mutations
- Handle loading, error, and success states properly
- Use proper error handling and retry logic

## UI Components
- Use Mantine UI components (`@mantine/core`, `@mantine/hooks`, etc.)
- Use `mantine-datatable` for data tables
- Follow Mantine design patterns and theming
- Use existing UI patterns and components

## State Management
- Use React Query for server state (API data)
- Use `useState` for local component state
- Use `useContext` for shared state when appropriate
- Avoid prop drilling - use context or state management library

## Error Handling
- Handle errors gracefully in UI
- Show user-friendly error messages
- Use proper null checks and optional chaining
- Handle loading states properly
- Don't crash on API errors - show error UI instead

## Code Style
- Follow ESLint and Prettier configurations
- Use consistent formatting (run `npm run prettier:write` before committing)
- Use meaningful variable and function names
- Keep functions focused and single-purpose
- Use proper indentation and spacing

## Import Organization
- React imports first
- Third-party library imports second
- Local imports last
- Use absolute imports when configured
- Group imports logically

## Testing
- Write tests for components when appropriate
- Use React Testing Library for component tests
- Test user interactions and edge cases
- Run tests before committing: `npm test`

## Documentation
- **DO NOT create summaries or documentation files unless explicitly requested**
- Add JSDoc comments for complex functions
- Document component props using TypeScript interfaces
- Explain complex logic in comments

## Performance
- Use React.memo for expensive components
- Use useMemo and useCallback when appropriate
- Avoid unnecessary re-renders
- Optimize API calls (use proper query keys, caching, etc.)
- Use code splitting for large components

## Routing
- Use React Router (`react-router-dom`) for navigation
- Follow existing route patterns
- Use proper route protection for authenticated routes
- Handle route parameters correctly

## Forms
- Use Mantine Form (`@mantine/form`) for form handling
- Validate forms properly
- Handle form submission and errors
- Use proper form state management

## Styling
- Use Mantine's styling system
- Use CSS modules or styled components when needed
- Follow existing styling patterns
- Keep styles organized and maintainable

## Accessibility
- Use proper semantic HTML
- Include ARIA labels when needed
- Ensure keyboard navigation works
- Test with screen readers when possible

## Build and Development
- Use `npm run dev` for development
- Use `npm run build` for production builds
- Use `npm run typecheck` to check TypeScript errors
- Use `npm run lint` to check code quality

